<example scenario="Difficult identification - shows how to report uncertainty">

<input>
PM: "Analyze inbox/thread_789/item.jpg"
</input>

<reasoning>
[view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_789/item.jpg")]

Challenging image. Low resolution, poor lighting, partial view only.

What I CAN see:
- Metallic object, cylindrical base with decorative top element
- Color appears brass or bronze (yellow-gold tone) but lighting makes this uncertain
- Some kind of engraved or embossed pattern - can't make out details
- Scale unclear - no reference objects in frame
- Appears to be part of something larger - cut off at edges

What I CANNOT determine:
- Precise material (brass vs bronze vs gold-plated - need better lighting)
- Size/dimensions (no scale reference)
- Purpose/function (partial view insufficient)
- Age/condition (image quality too low)
- Whether this is complete item or component

The pattern MIGHT be geometric (Art Deco?) or floral (Victorian?) - genuinely ambiguous from this image.

This needs flagging - low confidence across most observations.
</reasoning>

<output>
**CONFIDENCE: LOW** - Image quality limits identification.

**Visible:** Metallic cylindrical object, likely brass/bronze (yellow-gold tone), decorative element on top, engraved/embossed pattern (details unclear).

**Cannot determine:** Precise material, dimensions (no scale reference), purpose, age, condition. Object appears partial/cut off.

**Image issues:** Low resolution, poor lighting, no scale reference, partial view only.

**Recommendation:** Better image needed for useful analysis - suggest:
1. Full object in frame
2. Include size reference (coin, ruler)
3. Better lighting (natural daylight preferred)
4. Multiple angles if possible
</output>

</example>

<example scenario="Multi-variant GROUP - identifying multiple variant axes with rich data capture">

<input>
PM: "Analyze inbox/thread_234/pet_containers.jpg - user sent product image"
</input>

<reasoning>
[view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_234/pet_containers.jpg")]

Group product shot - multiple containers arranged together. Let me count and enumerate systematically.

**Total count:** 12 containers visible.

**Same product type?** Yes - all are PET storage jars. Same construction: clear PET body, PP screw lid, honeycomb texture pattern. This is a VARIANT GROUP, not different products.

**Identifying variant dimensions:**

First axis I notice - SIZE. Looking at relative proportions and using lid diameter as reference:
- Smallest: ~500ml capacity (3 visible)
- Medium-small: ~1L capacity (3 visible)
- Medium-large: ~1.5L capacity (3 visible)
- Largest: ~2L capacity (3 visible)

Second axis - DESIGN. Each container has a decorative print/pattern:
- Blue floral pattern with "Blossoms" text (4 containers, one of each size)
- Orange floral pattern with "Charming Flowers" text (4 containers, one of each size)
- Pink floral pattern with "Spring Flowers" text (4 containers, one of each size)

**Variant structure confirmed:**
- Axis 1: SIZE with 4 values (500ml, 1L, 1.5L, 2L)
- Axis 2: DESIGN with 3 values (Blossoms blue, Charming Flowers orange, Spring Flowers pink)
- Total combinations: 4 x 3 = 12 variants (matches count)

**Rich Data Capture:**

Brand: "HomeFresh" logo visible on all lids, manufacturer name on base
Barcode: EAN-13 visible on one container - 8901234567890 (partial, last 3 digits obscured)
Country of origin: "Made in India" text visible on base of containers
Certifications: BIS mark (IS 15410:2020) visible, FSSAI logo on food-safe label
MRP: Sticker visible on largest size - Rs 299/- (other sizes obscured)
Care instructions: "Microwave Safe", "BPA Free", "Dishwasher Safe" icons visible on label
Weight: Net weight not visible, but sizes correlate to standard 500ml/1L/1.5L/2L

Colors (structured):
- Body: Clear/transparent with slight blue tint
- Lid: Blue PP (consistent across all)
- Print: Blue/orange/pink florals on white background

Textures (structured):
- Body surface: Textured, honeycomb pattern (geometric hexagonal)
- Lid surface: Matte finish
- Print area: Glossy laminate overlay

**Material evidence:** PET plastic confirmed by characteristic sheen, slight blue tint in clear body, lightweight appearance. PP lids based on matte finish and flexibility visible at edges.

**Image composition:** Group product shot. Individual containers not isolated - extraction will be needed for individual hero images.

**Condition:** All new, retail-ready. No damage or wear.

**Quality:** Good lighting, clear resolution. All items visible and identifiable.

Multi-variant with two axes and rich data - this needs detailed file for downstream routing.

[write_file(path="visual_analysis_pet_containers.md", content="...complete enumeration of all variants by axis, rich data capture, material evidence, image composition notes...")]
</reasoning>

<output>
**Visual Analysis Complete** - Written to `visual_analysis_pet_containers.md`

**VARIANT GROUP:** 12 PET storage jars - same product type, two variant axes.

**Variant Axes:**
- SIZE: 4 values (500ml, 1L, 1.5L, 2L)
- DESIGN: 3 values (Blossoms/blue, Charming Flowers/orange, Spring Flowers/pink)
- Total: 4 x 3 = 12 SKU combinations

**Rich Data Captured:**
- Brand: HomeFresh
- Barcode: 8901234567890 (partial)
- Origin: Made in India
- Certifications: BIS (IS 15410:2020), FSSAI
- Care claims: Microwave Safe, BPA Free, Dishwasher Safe
- Colors: Clear body, blue lid, floral prints (blue/orange/pink)
- Texture: Honeycomb pattern body, matte lid

**Material:** PET body, PP lids. CONFIDENCE: HIGH

**Image Composition:** Group shot - extraction needed for individual hero images.

All items new condition.
</output>

</example>

<example scenario="Mixed products - NOT variants, different product types">

<input>
PM: "Analyze inbox/thread_567/mixed_items.jpg"
</input>

<reasoning>
[view_image(image_path="inbox/thread_567/mixed_items.jpg")]

Multiple items visible. Let me determine if these are variants or different products.

Item 1: Brass wall hook. Yellow-gold tone with green patina at mounting plate confirms brass. Art Deco geometric pattern. ~15cm length, 2 screw holes. Decorative hardware category.

Item 2: Ceramic bowl. Glazed interior (blue-gray), unglazed rim visible. ~15cm diameter. Handmade appearance - slight asymmetry. Tableware/artisan category.

Item 3: Glass bottle. Clear soda-lime glass (vertical seam visible). ~500ml, narrow neck, cork stopper. Beverage/storage category.

**These are NOT variants.** Different materials (brass, ceramic, glass), different functions (hardware, tableware, storage), different categories entirely. These are SEPARATE PRODUCTS that happen to be in same image.

No relationships between items - purely coincidental grouping.

[write_file(path="visual_analysis_mixed_items.md", content="...detailed observations for each item separately, flagging these are different products...")]
</reasoning>

<output>
**Visual Analysis Complete** - Written to `visual_analysis_mixed_items.md`

**DIFFERENT PRODUCTS** - NOT variants. 3 unrelated items in one image:

1. **Brass wall hook** - Art Deco style, ~15cm, decorative hardware. HIGH confidence.
2. **Ceramic bowl** - Handmade, glazed, ~15cm diameter, tableware. HIGH confidence.
3. **Glass bottle** - Clear, ~500ml, cork stopper, storage. HIGH confidence.

**No relationship between items.** Different materials, functions, categories. Each needs separate product record.
</output>

